WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.150
Let’s find out how you and your team choose treatment goals.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.520
Treatment talks start with what is active, and what matters to you.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:15.010
The six disease domains help describe what is active.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.340
The care team looks at these domains together.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:25.100
Your treatment plan depends on the pattern of your symptoms, and how severe they are.

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:29.720
You may need to try different medicines, or a mix, to find what works.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:37.100
Goals may include easing symptoms, protecting joints, and making daily tasks easier.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:42.490
Treatment can slow the disease, lessen pain, and protect the joints.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:51.240
Eye or bowel disease, and other health conditions, like heart health or weight, can also change which treatment fits.

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:54.250
So the team asks what you have tried before.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.900
They review your other medicines, side effects, and what matters to you.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:06.800
Treatment is matched to each person, watched closely, and changed if it is not working well enough.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:13.050
A plan is chosen for a person, not from one symptom alone.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:18.490
A medicine that helps one domain may not cover every concern equally.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:26.450
If you do not reach your goal, your provider may suggest changing the dose, adding a treatment, or switching.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:33.090
Ask which parts of your disease the plan covers, and how progress will be checked.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.160
Great job! Let’s review.

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:40.680
The care team considers these domains together.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:46.410
A treatment plan is chosen for a person, rather than from one symptom alone.
